    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῦμα</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρύω</span>
		(A)) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is drawn</i>:
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξου ῥ.</span>, i.e. the Persian
				<i>archers</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγχης
			ἰσχύς</span>, i.e. the Greek spearmen, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				147
			</span></i> (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τόξου
			ῥύματος</span> from the distance of a bow-<i>shot</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.3.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τόξου ῥ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eun.
					<u>Hist.</u>
					p.271D.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>towing-line</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.26.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.46.5
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				3.44
			</span></i>.</div>
